<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33430" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pālārĭs</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		1. palus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to pales</i>
			or <i>stakes</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">silva palaris,</span>”
				<i>from which pales are fetched</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					7, 1, 9</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pālārĭa</span></b> ,
				ĭum, n., <i>the exercise of tilting against a stake;</i> also, <i>the place of this exercise</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Veg. Mil. 1, 11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2,
			23</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Charis. p. 21</span></i>
		P.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
